+Cluster input: `tests/fixtures/golden/help/setup.txt`, slice `slices/000108.diff`. The slice is identical to `git diff` of the path over the captured range: a one-sentence addition to the Hermes scope note of `setup --help`.
+
+## What the change says
+
+The golden now adds, after the 0.22.1 passthrough requirement: "a launcher that sets HERDR_THREADS_CONTINUITY_KEY lists it there too". It is the expected output of `golden_surfaces::help_texts`, which records `setup --help` byte for byte.
+
+## Checks against the producer
+
+- Producer match: the whole `setup_scope` string of `src/harness/hermes.rs` at head (1423 bytes) occurs verbatim in the golden, including the rewrapped lines.
+- Accuracy against the bridge: at head, `HERDR_THREADS_CONTINUITY_KEY` is in `PANE_ENV` of `integrations/hermes/__init__.py`. In the shared gateway the bridge drops `PANE_ENV` names from the gateway's `os.environ` and takes them only from the session's client env, which `terminal.client_env_passthrough` carries. So a key not listed never reaches the hook, as the sentence says. `integrations/hermes/test_bridge.py` pins that a gateway-level key does not leak into a bound session.
+- Accuracy against the spec: the design's client-side section has the Hermes bridge add the key to `PANE_ENV`. `integrations/hermes/README.md` carries the same instruction in the same words, so the two operator surfaces agree.
+- Layout: the new lines are 84 and 73 columns, within the block's existing width (up to 86).
+- Test evidence: the task 7 report records the `golden` filter passing on tree 788f79169d2a40271bf8a843cb46abcda330ad08. Between that tree and head, the golden, `src/harness/hermes.rs` and `tests/golden_surfaces.rs` have identical blobs, and `src/cli/mod.rs`, `src/cli/commands.rs`, `src/cli/help.rs`, `src/cli/setup.rs` and `src/harness/` have no diff. I reuse that evidence and did not rebuild for one fixture line.
+- Token rules: this is static help text shown only when `setup --help` is asked for, not per-delivery framing. Commit 7a87f5209 says "No new model-visible string" about the hook refusal texts; the help sentence is 70 bytes and is not one of those texts. The commit's `Outside-adapter` trailer lists the golden.
